{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Blessing of breasts and womb.</b> He likened the heavens to breasts, and the earth to a womb. Another interpretation: <b>blessing of breasts</b> — that they not shrivel and that the children not die for lack of milk. <b>And womb</b> — even within the womb the fetus shall not die. Here he put breasts before womb, because the milk habitually comes to a woman's breasts before her delivery; but Hosea said ״תן להם רחם משכיל״ before he said ״ושדים צומקים״ — that is, give them that they not give birth, and if they do give birth, their breasts shall shrivel and they will not be able to nurse."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:17.265169720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}